    {
      "entity": 17592186571448,
      "attribute": ":question/problem",
      "value": "Consider the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is upper triangular\n\nII. $A$ is lower triangular\n\nIII. ${A}^{T}$ is lower triangular",
      "tx": 13194139536397,
      "basis": 3085,
      "source": ":org/Math-Academy",
      "added": true
    },
    {
      "entity": 17592186571448,
      "attribute": ":question/id",
      "value": "e901e3e2-6ad0-5a4e-b4c9-fb5111610c41",
      "tx": 13194139536397,
      "basis": 3085,
      "source": ":org/Math-Academy",
      "added": true
    },
    {
      "entity": 17592186571448,
      "attribute": ":question/worked-solution",
      "value": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false, since ${A}^{T}$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None\".",
      "tx": 13194139536397,
      "basis": 3085,
      "source": ":org/Math-Academy",
      "added": true
    }
  ],
